# Both AI tools (deck evaluator + website reviewer) call Claude through
# Vercel AI Gateway (lib/ai.ts, model "anthropic/claude-opus-5"), not the
# Anthropic API directly. No key is required in most cases:
#
# - On a real Vercel deployment: nothing to set here at all. Vercel injects a
#   VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN into every function invocation automatically, and the
#   gateway uses it to authenticate — as long as AI Gateway is enabled for
#   the project (Vercel dashboard -> Project -> Settings -> AI Gateway).
# - For local dev against your real Vercel project: run `vercel link` once,
#   then `vercel env pull .env.local` — this writes a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN into
#   .env.local for you (valid ~24h; re-run `vercel env pull` when it expires).
#   Leave AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY below blank in this case.
# - For any other host (CI, a non-Vercel server, or if you'd rather not use
#   `vercel link` locally): set AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY instead, from the Vercel
#   dashboard's AI Gateway settings. The gateway checks this before falling
#   back to VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Required outside Vercel (local dev, this sandbox, or any other host):
# point this at a real Chromium binary. Install one locally with
# `npx playwright install chromium`, then set this to the path it reports.
# On Vercel, leave this unset — lib/screenshot.ts detects the VERCEL env var
# (set automatically by the platform) and uses @sparticuz/chromium instead.
PLAYWRIGHT_EXECUTABLE_PATH=
